WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.260
Local LLM infrastructure is a systems-engineering problem.

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:09.128
It combines CPU, GPU, VRAM or unified memory, system RAM, storage, power, cooling,

00:00:09.128 --> 00:00:13.190
operating system, drivers, runtime, model, interfaces, security, and maintenance.

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:18.155
Local and cloud inference offer different control, capability, cost, scaling, privacy,

00:00:18.155 --> 00:00:19.510
and operational tradeoffs.

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:23.121
Choose according to measured requirements rather than ideology.

00:00:23.121 --> 00:00:27.635
Model fit depends on parameters, architecture, quantization, context, cache, concurrency,

00:00:27.635 --> 00:00:28.989
offload, and overhead.

00:00:28.989 --> 00:00:34.857
A model that loads is not necessarily stable or useful under real demand.

00:00:34.857 --> 00:00:39.822
Start with a simple supported stack, trusted model source, known configuration,

00:00:39.822 --> 00:00:42.530
representative benchmark, and clear acceptance criteria.

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:47.044
Measure prompt processing, generation, latency, quality, memory, thermals, and failures.

00:00:47.044 --> 00:00:52.461
Protect APIs, accounts, networks, prompts, documents, logs, backups, and model supply chains.

00:00:52.461 --> 00:00:57.426
Scale only when a real workload justifies more hardware or orchestration.

00:00:57.426 --> 00:01:01.940
Strong local systems are maintainable, secure, measured, and appropriately modest.
